1. What this license covers

This license applies to the files in the `ee/` directory of the MonitorFlow
repository and to anything built from them (the "Enterprise Code"). Every
file outside `ee/` is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later, and nothing here changes that. Releases of MonitorFlow
already published, and every version of the repository before the
Enterprise Code was added, stay under the AGPL as they were published.

"We" and "us" mean the copyright holder named above. "You" means the person
or organisation using the Enterprise Code. A "Subscription" is a paid
MonitorFlow Enterprise subscription from us that is current. A "License Key"
is the signed file we deliver with a Subscription, stating who it is for,
how many central servers it allows and until when.

2. What you may do without a Subscription

You may, free of charge:

  a. read the Enterprise Code, and copy it;
  b. change it, build it, and run it, for development, testing,
     demonstration and evaluation, without a time limit, as long as that
     use is not production use;
  c. share copies of the Enterprise Code, changed or not, with others, as
     long as this license goes with them, unchanged, and every changed file
     says that you changed it;
  d. contribute changes back to us, under the MonitorFlow Contributor
     License Agreement (see CONTRIBUTING.md), on the same terms as
     contributions to the rest of MonitorFlow.

"Production use" means using the Enterprise Code to watch, manage or update
machines for any purpose other than development, testing, demonstration or
evaluation: in short, relying on it.

3. Production use

Production use of the Enterprise Code needs a Subscription and its License
Key, within the limits the License Key states: the number of central
servers and the period. When the Subscription ends or the License Key
expires, you may keep running the central servers you had already added
under it, as the software itself allows, but you may not add others.

4. What you may not do

You may not:

  a. remove, disable or work around the License Key check in the
     Enterprise Code, or change the Enterprise Code so that it runs in
     production beyond what your License Key allows;
  b. sell, rent or host the Enterprise Code for others as a service, or
     sell access to features it provides, without a written agreement with
     us;
  c. remove or change this license, copyright notices, or the notices of
     the license on screen.

Building MonitorFlow without the Enterprise Code (the server's Cargo
feature `enterprise` turned off), and running the AGPL code alone, is
governed by the AGPL only. This license does not restrict it in any way.

5. Combining with the AGPL code

The Enterprise Code is made to be combined with the AGPL code of MonitorFlow
into one program. We permit that combination, and its distribution, as
`ee/README.md` describes. Your rights to the AGPL parts of such a program
come from the AGPL; your rights to the Enterprise parts come from this
license.

6. Patents

Each contributor grants you a licence, under any patent claims they can
license and that the contribution necessarily infringes, to use the
Enterprise Code as this license allows. That licence ends for you if you
claim in court that the Enterprise Code infringes a patent.

7. No warranty

The Enterprise Code is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. Any
warranty, support or service level comes only from the terms of a
Subscription.

8. Limitation of liability

To the extent the law allows, we and the contributors are not liable for
any damage arising from the Enterprise Code or its use, unless the terms of
a Subscription say otherwise.

9. Ending

If you break this license, your rights under it end. They come back if you
stop within 30 days of our notice, the first time it happens. Ending does
not affect the AGPL code.

10. Changes

We may publish new versions of this license. Code published under one
version stays available under that version.
